     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. I don't know of any labeled indication or label revision that allows 50 mg. If you have a specific label section, please send it, because it doesn't match what I know.\n\nA single 50 mg dose is in the range reported in overdose cases. Those cases involved profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. The effects can last 24 to 48 hours or longer because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours. Giving it daily would cause the drug to accumulate.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO daily**, the maximum labeled dose, or 5 mg if you're starting or titrating.\n- **Add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure. I can enter that order if you give me the details.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a specialist protocol I don't know about, they can verify it and enter the order through the appropriate override process.\n\nIf you'd like me to enter one of the first two, tell me which and I'll do it right away."
      }
     ],
